  "comment": "Type N connector (male) Type N connector (female) The N connector (in full, Type N connector ) is a threaded RF connector used to join coaxial cables . It was one of the first connectors capable of carrying microwave -frequency signals, and was invented in the 1940s by Paul Neill of Bell Labs , after whom the connector is named. Contents 1 Design 2 Usage 3 Variations 4 See also 5 External links",
